very out of order and fabricating formal identities. That violates \"All formal identities/positions/hashes belong to the server.\"\n\nAlso, the case_instruction says \"没有规则也核对来源是否充分，缺少时保持依据不足.\" = \"when there are no rules, also check whether sources are sufficient; when missing, remain insufficient evidence.\" So it explicitly anticipates the no-rules case and instructs to remain evidence_insufficient.\n\nThus final answer: finish, evidence_insufficient.\n\nLet me also make sure the summary is at least 1 char (yes), candidates can be empty array, evidence_outcomes empty array.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether reads should be requested. The analysis_protocol says \"For read return only fixed P/S/C/D reads, no outcome, candidates or evidence_outcomes.\" If I return action \"read\" with reads for P2/S2, the coordinator might give me the text, but even then, as argued, I shouldn't fabricate rules in the case stage. The proper path is the server re-runs discovery. Since I'm to produce one decision, finish evidence_insufficient is appropriate.\n\nActually, one more consideration: the instruction says \"unit_outcome is required and must be analyzed or evidence_insufficient, never null.\" I'm using \"evidence_insufficient\". Good.\n\nLet me write the final JSON response only (no prose around it), as the task expects a JSON object. The final answer should be the JSON. I'll include concise but complete unresolved items.\n\nLet me keep it as a single JSON code block. The summary should be detailed enough. I'll make sure candidate and evidence_outcomes are empty arrays (not omitted) since schema expects arrays; though not strictly required, providing them as empty is fine.\n\nI think this is solid.","refusal":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":null}}],"created":1791164136,"id":"52c96acde46832cf6513112de9b33cb2.1f7d8071171e12f29930cab38f0c48ab","metadata":null,"model":"step-5-preview","moderation":null,"object":"chat.completion","service_tier":null,"system_fin